Initial investigation focuses on the telemetry implementation within the specified component, specifically lines 370-387. The code uses a state hook and an effect hook to fetch telemetry data from a JSON endpoint. The goal is to understand how this mechanism currently works.

The effect hook fetches telemetry data every three seconds, storing it in gpuTelemetry. This data, specifically is_active and vram_used_mb, is then used conditionally in the rendering. Conditional rendering occurs within a span for the active status and within another span for VRAM usage. The rendering demonstrates the status and VRAM usage of the RTX 4090 Core.

The code now attempts to render additional GPU metrics: power, temperature, and system RAM usage. Suspecting a similar data fetching pattern, examining the data flow for these new metrics is the next step. If these new values are undefined, this hints that the telemetry endpoint may not provide those fields.

